* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
# Byte-for-byte copies and generated output: their checksums and drift checks compare LF bytes,
# so a Windows checkout must not rewrite them.
contract/** text eol=lf
scenarios/** text eol=lf
typescript/src/generated/** text eol=lf

# THE CONTRACT IS SWEPT BY SCRIPTS, AND `* text=auto` ABOVE MADE THAT A TRAP (I2a,
# ATLAS-592). With core.autocrlf=true this file checked out CRLF on Windows while its
# blob stayed LF, so a Node sweep anchored on `\n` matched NOTHING and reported a clean
# run having changed nothing - which is exactly what #534 records happening twice. The
# blob is already LF, so this line changes no bytes; it stops the working tree and the
# blob disagreeing, for every sweep after this one.
packages/api-spec/openapi.yaml text eol=lf
*.webp binary
*.mp4 binary
# A RECORDED RUN'S EVIDENCE IS ITS BYTES (J3e, ATLAS-722). Its report cites each snapshot's SHA-256, and
# `* text=auto` would check the files out CRLF on Windows and change every hash. The blobs are LF as read.
docs/performance/*/*.json text eol=lf
docs/performance/*/*.txt text eol=lf
apps/web/public/media/*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
